Comment: The eight citizens of Uruk (villagers, townspeople, nobles) are made like Ishtar: concept images from InvokeAI
 (Juggernaut XL v9, models-src/rodin/make_concepts.py and img2img_concept.py), turned into 3D models by Hyper3D Rodin (Gen-2.5-High),
 then rigged by models-src/rodin_rig.py. The terms of use of Hyper3D must be checked before distribution.

Files: media/models/scorpion_man.glb media/models/bull_of_heaven.glb media/portraits/scorpion_man.jpg media/portraits/bull_of_heaven.jpg
 models-src/scorpion_man/* models-src/bull_of_heaven/* models-src/rodin/scorpion_man.json models-src/rodin/bull_of_heaven.json
Copyright: 2026 Ishtaria Team <ishtaria@vitexsoftware.com>
License: CC-BY-SA-4.0
Comment: The two creatures are generated meshes: the Bull of Heaven from one InvokeAI concept, the Scorpion Man assembled by
 models-src/rodin_scorpion_assemble.py from two Rodin meshes (a giant scorpion and the upper body of a bearded man, each from
 its own InvokeAI concept), all made by Hyper3D Rodin (Gen-2.5-High) and rigged by models-src/rodin_rig_creature.py. The terms
 of use of Hyper3D must be checked before distribution.

Files: media/models/architecture/ziggurat_etemenanki.glb media/models/architecture/etemenanki_precinct.glb
 media/models/architecture/uruk_walls.glb media/models/architecture/uruk_walls_collision.glb
 media/models/architecture/uruk_quarter_*.glb media/models/architecture/uruk_market*.glb media/models/architecture/uruk_palace*.glb
 media/models/architecture/uruk_sinkashid*.glb media/models/architecture/uruk_ishtar_ziggurat.glb media/models/architecture/uruk_eanna*.glb
 media/models/architecture/ziggurat_anu.glb media/models/architecture/ishtar_gate.glb
 media/models/architecture/processional_way.glb models-src/architecture/*
Copyright: 2026 Ishtaria Team <ishtaria@vitexsoftware.com>
License: CC-BY-SA-4.0
Comment: Built by models-src/architecture/ziggurat.py (Blender). The brick, glaze, plaster and paving textures
 were generated with InvokeAI (Juggernaut XL v9) and made seamless by make_tileable.py. The designs follow the
 reconstructions described in research/ZIGGURATS.md and research/ISHTAR_GATE.md; no published illustration was copied or used
 as a reference image. The animal reliefs of the Ishtar Gate are new drawings generated for this datadisk.
 The streets, houses, markets, palaces and fields of Uruk are planned by tools/build_city.py (tools/data/uruk_city.json) and
 built by uruk_city.py and uruk_sites.py; the textures of the clay-cone mosaic (make_cone_mosaic.py) and of the furrowed fields
 (make_field_textures.py) are drawn by those scripts after the descriptions of the patterns, not copied from any picture. The
 layout follows the excavation as described in research/CITY.md.

Files: media/models/architecture/burney_relief.glb models-src/burney_relief/* models-src/architecture/burney_relief.py models-src/architecture/burney_restore.py
Copyright: danielpett (https://sketchfab.com/danielpett), photogrammetry scan of the Burney Relief (British Museum)
License: CC-BY-4.0
Comment: This work is based on "The Burney Relief"
 (https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/the-burney-relief-217a01bf2d324ad19a05e54256b2824e) by danielpett, licensed under CC-BY-4.0
 (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); the original licence text is models-src/burney_relief/license.txt. Changes: the six
 pieces are joined, decimated from 500000 to 45000 faces, the textures are scaled down to 2048 px and the model is scaled, moved and
 turned to stand upright, the broken right half of the head is mirrored from the surviving left half, the slab is removed and the back is closed
 (models-src/architecture/burney_restore.py, notes in models-src/burney_relief/RESTORATION.md). The adaptation is distributed here under
 CC-BY-SA-4.0.

Files: media/models/architecture/lamassu_pair.glb media/models/architecture/lamassu_pair_collision.glb media/models/architecture/shedu_pair.glb media/models/architecture/shedu_pair_collision.glb models-src/lamassu/* models-src/architecture/lamassu_models.py models-src/rodin_lamassu_assemble.py models-src/concepts/lamassu_*
